bency, cash and a favorable post-redistricting map, and markets plus most raters put him clearly ahead. But the R-tilting district, Tijerina's serious campaign and corruption-focused attacks keep this short of Likely D.", "watch": "Any late independent polling or a major scandal development could shift the race toward Tijerina or lock in Cuellar.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Henry Cuellar (D) is running."]}, "overview": "South Texas's 28th District pairs a ten-term incumbent Democrat, Henry Cuellar, against Webb County Judge Tano Tijerina, a Republican convert running with visible national party support. The district's partisan lean favors Republicans by about three points, but new redistricting lines and Cuellar's incumbency have historically cushioned him. A single August poll showed Cuellar up eleven points, though polling here is sparse and older surveys have been volatile.\n\nMost professional raters place the race between Tilt D and Likely D, and prediction markets price Cuellar's win chances near 89 percent. Tijerina has raised nearly $1.4 million and campaigned alongside Trump, keeping Republican attention on the seat. The forecast expects Cuellar to win by a modest margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the district's shifting Latino electorate.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9009, "margin": 7.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8779, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8804, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8617, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8968, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9013, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9125, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8966, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8974, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10